<ns0:para xmlns:ns0="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:ns1="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="fs-id1167836293187">We used the equation <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>−</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>3</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> and its graph as we developed the vertical line test. We said that the relation defined by the equation <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>−</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>3</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> is a function.</ns0:para>
